    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "# Build Status States\r\n\r\n**Goal:** Make your app communicate clearly when data is loading, missing, or broken.\r\n\r\nImport your status message sketch from Level 8 so you can use it as a guide while building your loading, error, and empty states.\r\n\r\n## Add Your Status States\r\n\r\nUpdate your app so it:\r\n\r\n- shows a loading message or indicator as soon as the user requests data\r\n- hides the loading state after the data loads\r\n- uses `try` / `catch` to handle API errors\r\n- shows a helpful error message if the API fails\r\n- checks for empty or invalid results\r\n- shows a helpful empty state message instead of leaving the page blank\r\n- hides the error or empty message when valid results appear again\r\n\r\n## Test as You Build\r\n\r\nClick your button and confirm that the loading state appears right away and disappears when results show.\r\n\r\nTemporarily break your API URL to confirm that your error message appears.\r\n\r\nModify your endpoint or search input to force zero results and confirm that your empty state appears.",
